// RED PIN (auto-discharge bug, found 2026-06-12): two live resources that must
// BOTH be discharged on one path can only be freed by chaining the disposals in
// one pipeline (`free(s2) |> free(s1)`) — String can't auto-discharge (free/take
// are both candidates, KORU030), so every resource needs an EXPLICIT free, and
// two live resources means two explicit frees on the path.
//
// The auto-discharge checker mis-handles this: it recognizes a SINGLE explicit
// disposal per continuation but not two chained in one `|>` pipeline. The walk
// still believes one resource leaks and tries to auto-insert a disposal for it,
// failing on the free/take ambiguity with a FALSE KORU030. Confirmed general
// (independent of substring) — any two live resources hit it.
//
// This blocks all multi-resource flows (strings, files, connections). Greens
// when checkContinuation recognizes every explicit disposal in a chained
// pipeline, clearing each obligation. See src/auto_discharge_inserter.zig
// (checkContinuation / checkInvocationSatisfiesObligations, the chained-
// continuation recursion).
~import std/string
~import std/io

~std/string:from-page(text: "a")
| ok s1 |> std/string:from-page(text: "b")
    | ok s2 |> std/string:read(s2)
        | slice t |> std/io:print.ln("{{ t:s }}") |> std/string:free(s2) |> std/string:free(s1)
    | err _ |> std/string:free(s1)
| err _ |> _
